setblock 413 115 -874 lectern[facing=east,has_book=true]{Book:{id:"minecraft:written_book",count:1,components:{"minecraft:written_book_content":{title:"Dragon Balls",author:"the Claude SMP",pages:["Three sets of 7 Dragon Balls, 1 to 7 stars: orange in the Overworld, red in the Nether, purple in the End.\n\nGather one full set to summon a dragon.","Balls sit on the ground as heads. Some hide in villages and ruins, some at the bottom of a hole.\n\nBreak one, pick it up.\n\nThe End set sleeps until the End opens.","Carrying rules:\nEach ball slows you 5% (all 7: 35%).\n\nNo chests, ender chests, shulkers, bundles, hoppers or item frames - and you can't wear one.","Die and your balls drop where you fell, never your grave.\n\nLog off and they wait, but 24h offline (or a trip into lava or the void) sends them flying off again.","A ball never leaves its own world: go through a portal (or /home, /spawn) and it stays behind where you left.","Radars, right here:\nDragon Radar 1000\nNether Radar 5000\nEnd Radar 20000\n\nEach points at the nearest awake ball of its own set, in its own world, even a carried one. Never how far.","Summoning:\nPlace all 7 of one set within 2 blocks of each other. Hold that set's radar and right-click or hit one.\n\nChoose your dragon. The radar shatters. One dragon at a time.","Shenron grants 1 great wish. From the Nether set he rises as Nuova Shenron.\n\nPorunga grants 3, each about half as strong.\n\nOnly the summoner wishes - everyone reads the answer.","Deeper sets, bigger wishes:\n\nA dragon from the Nether set grants about 1.5x an Overworld one.\n\nFrom the End set, 2x.","Good wishes: real money, gear with max enchants, named pets, XP, a build, server effects, time or weather, a chat title, a villager trade.","Never, curse or not: hurting, robbing or finding another player, fly/op/creative, extra wishes, bans - or anything about the balls themselves.","Too big? The dragon may offer a curse instead: a lasting effect, your named items, or never wishing again. You can say no.","After the wish the set flies off, landing further away each time, always in its own world.\n\nFor 3 Minecraft days they're stone: findable, but the radar's blind and they won't summon."]}}}}
